## Orient and assess

- Read relevant source pages and maps under the memory root. Follow relative links from the current page's directory.
- Inventory shared `memories/*.md` pages and the active project's own `memories/projects/<project-key>/*.md` pages. Other project folders are out of scope. Maps are navigation, not factual sources. Do not create legacy USER.md or MEMORY.md.
- Find overlapping notes with `grep` and `glob`; read full source pages before proposing a consolidation. Avoid rereading the entire corpus when only a few topics changed.
- Preserve project scope, user corrections, unique constraints, provenance, verification results and unresolved issues. A newer timestamp alone does not prove a claim true.
- Keep `agent.md`, `HABITS.md`, project instructions, histories and backups unchanged. Preserve `<!-- nova-memory-wiki:checklist -->` and its checklist sections. Do not retire or rewrite source pages.

## Stage proposals, never edit pages

- Use `propose_memory_lesson(topic, content, scope, evidence)` for every semantic wiki change. Its content must be substantive Markdown bullets, with evidence paths to the source pages.
- The tool only creates a pending, version-specific proposal. It does not write or edit a page. Report its `id@revision`; the user must approve it through `/learning` before it is applied.
- Choose `project` scope only for the active project's own notes. Choose `shared` only for facts genuinely useful across projects. Never move a project-specific fact into shared memory.
- Include useful summary, tags and related-page links in the proposed Markdown bullets when they improve retrieval. Links must be relative to the destination topic page and point to existing pages.
- Do not call `write_file`, `edit_file`, or `delete_file`. They are intentionally unavailable for persistent memory during a dream.
- If no semantic addition is justified, create no proposal and say so. Do not restate existing notes as new lessons.

## Verify and report

- `memory_wiki(action="maintain")` rebuilds only deterministic navigation from actual pages. It may add indexes, maps and navigation links, but does not edit semantic page bodies.
- Call `memory_wiki(action="check")`; report unresolved links without inventing target pages.
- Report the source pages reviewed, each staged proposal reference and scope, and any unresolved conflict. Distinguish navigation maintenance from approved semantic edits.
